-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",452,{
[14433]="700017C5\n1\tDefeat Wargs in Annúndir and investigate Haudh Eglan\tHaudh Eglan lies north of a cliff called \"Amlaith's Scar,\" which likewise lies west of Ost Lagoros in Annúndir. You should defeat Wargs and search Haudh Eglan.\n2\tSearch the burial mound of Haudh Eglan\030Defeat Wargs in Annúndir (total: 8)\tHaudh Eglan lies north of a cliff called \"Amlaith's Scar,\" which likewise lies west of Ost Lagoros in Annúndir. You should defeat Wargs and search Haudh Eglan.\n3\tTalk to Orthonn\tOrthonn can be found at Ost Lagoros, bordering the eastern edge of Annúndir (across the river). You should bring news of Haudh Eglan to Orthonn.\n",
[14434]="7001ABA4\n1\tDefeat Wargs (total: 20)\tKill Wargs in Draugdegil.\n",
[14435]="70015E3E\n1\tDefeat shadow-wargs (total: 14)\tThe shadow-wargs inhabit the Burnt Tor, west of Ruidhriel. Ruidhriel has asked that you kill the Wargs that stalk the Burnt Tor.\n2\tTalk to Ruidhriel\tRuidhriel is east of the Burnt Tor. You should return to Ruidhriel and tell her of your success.\n",
[14436]="7000EAA8\n1\tCollect Peikko hides (total: 18)\tPeikko can be found north of Sûri-kylä. Nôra has asked you to collect Peikko hides to help supplement the bear-furs you collected for her already.\n2\tTalk to Nôra\030Collect Peikko-hide (total: 18)\tNôra is at Sûri-kylä, south from where you found the Peikko. You should return to Nôra with the hides you collected.\n",
[14437]="70003817\n1\tBring the wolf-pelts to Dorri in Gondamon\030Collect wolf-pelts (total: 5)\tWolves can be found in the wilds around Gondamon, especially to the west. Dorri has asked you to hunt the wolves that menace the wilds around Gondamon and obtain pelts he can use to make blankets and winter clothing.\n",
[14438]="7005B10F\n1\tCollect wolf pelts (total: 6)\030Collect bear pelts (total: 6)\030Collect Warg pelts (total: 6)\tBears, Wargs, and wolves can be found throughout the woods of Azanulbizar. Thorin has tasked you with collecting animal pelts to help keep warm the Haban'akkâ of Thráin.\n2\tDeliver the pelts to Thorin at Amdân\tThorin can be found at Amdân. You should deliver the pelts to Thorin.\n",
[14439]="70020BB6\n1\tCollect wolf-pelts (total: 10)\tWolves may be found throughout the Windfells of Enedwaith. Andreg has asked you to hunt the wolves of the Windfells for their warm pelts, which may be used as a defence against the cold of winter.\n2\tBring wolf-pelts to Saeradan at Echad Saeradan\tSaeradan is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith. Andreg told you to bring the wolf-pelts to Saeradan to be prepared for delivery to the Algraig.\n",
[14440]="7002BFCB\n1\tTalk to Aculf at his camp in the Rushgore\tAculf is at his camp in the Rushgore, west of the Woodman camp. You should bring Amal's warning to Aculf.\n",
[14441]="7000178E\n1\tTalk to Amarion\tAmarion is at his camp atop Amon Raith, east of the Fields of Fornost. Mincham believes the Orcs at Fornost have some greater plan than the occupation of the old ruins and has asked you to carry word of warning to Amarion, a young Ranger assigned to keep watch upon Amon Raith.\n",
[14442]="700529D6\n1\tWarn Begga\030Warn Evrul\030Warn Gudule\030Warn Hodver\tThe Woodmen Begga, Evrul, Gudule, and Hodver live in the Wolf-denes, south of Vegbár. You should find them and send them to safety before the goblins come for them!\n2\tTalk to Langhár\tLanghár can be summoned to your side with Langhár's summoning horn. You should talk to Langhár. If Langhár is no longer with you, she may be outside Waldfast or in Vegbár.\n",
[14443]="70007DF0\n1\tPost Vighar's sign outside the northern entrance to Gabilazan\tThe pass of Gabilazan is south-west of the High Crag camp atop a slope. Vighar Roadwalker has given you a sign to post just outside the northern entrance to the pass of Gabilazan. Evil dwarves have occupied the keep that guards the pass.\n2\tTalk to Vighar Roadwalker\tVighar Roadwalker is at the High Crag camp, north-east of Gabilazan. Vighar will be pleased to hear that you have posted the sign he gave you in front of the pass of Gabilazan, guarded by Dourhands.\n",
[14444]="70007DF1\n1\tPost Vighar's sign in the pass of Rakhâs-bizar\tThe pass of Rakhâs-bizar is east of the pass of Gabilazan, where you posted Vighar's sign warning of the Dourhands. Vighar Roadwalker has given you a sign to post in the pass of Rakhâs-bizar, warning of giants to the south. He advised you not to attempt this task on your own.\n2\tTalk to Vighar Roadwalker\tVighar Roadwalker is at the High Crag camp, north-east of Rivendell. Vighar will be pleased to hear that you have posted the sign he gave you in the pass of Rakhâs-bizar, north of the land of the giants.\n",
[14445]="70007DF2\n1\tPost Vighar's Sign outside the Rhudauran Keep\tEvil Men have established themselves in a keep to the north-west of the High Crag camp. Vighar Roadwalker has given you a sign to post just outside the entrance of the keep occupied by evil Men in the north-western Misty Mountains.\n2\tTalk to Vighar Roadwalker\tVighar Roadwalker is at the High Crag camp, east of Glóin's camp. Vighar will be pleased to hear that you have posted the sign he gave you in front of the keep occupied by evil Rhudaurans.\n",
[14446]="70028CAD\n1\tTalk to Innoth near the Isen\tInnoth can be found by travelling south until you reach the Isen, then east along the shore until you reach the rocky outcropping where Innoth is encamped. Garrun has sent you on to speak with Innoth near the river Isen.\n",
[14447]="7002EFE8\n1\tSpeak with Burnoth to help the Riders Four leave Cliving unnoticed\tBurnoth is encamped outside the Mead Hall of Cliving. You should speak with Burnoth when you are ready to aid him.\n2\tTalk to Reeve Athelward at the Mead Hall of Cliving\tReeve Athelward is in the Mead Hall of Cliving. Burnoth told you to let Reeve Athelward know that they have graciously declined his invitation and have continued their mission.\n",
[14448]="7000978E\n1\tSearch jetsam along the shore of Tinnudir (total: 6)\tJetsam from Lake Nenuial often washes onto the western shore of Tinnudir, north of the Ranger-camp. Astiul has asked you to follow the island's shore north of the Ranger-camp in search of jetsam and to search any you find for damp pottery shards.\n2\tBring damp pottery shards to Astiul\tAstiul is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir in Evendim, south of the jetsam-littered shore. The Ranger Astiul waits for you to return with the results of your search along the shore of Lake Nenuial.\n",
[14449]="70066A58\n1\tCollect freshly-cut logs at Fleetmire (total: 10)\tDardreg has asked you to collect freshly-cut logs left behind by Corsairs. These logs can be found scattered around Fleetmire, south-west of the lumber camp.\n2\tTalk to Dardreg at the lumber camp\tYou have gathered a good amount of logs. You should bring them back to Dardreg, who waits for you at the lumber camp.\n",
[14450]="70062DE2\n1\tCollect Tesni's dagger from one of the half-orc captains at Nímbarth\tOne of the half-orc captains at Nímbarth might have Tesni's dagger.\n2\tBring the blood-stained dagger to Tesni west of Nímbarth\tTesni watches over Nímbarth from a safe distance.\n",
[14451]="7002FF04\n1\tDefeat roots along the Entwash (total: 12)\tRoots can be found along the Entwash in Fangorn. You should defeat treacherous roots along the river-banks.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have cleared many of the treacherous tangling roots growing along the Entwash.\n",
[14452]="70047BDB\n1\tTalk to Mincham\tMincham can be found at Tham Durlan in south-western Dagorlad. Artamir has asked you to speak to Mincham about allowing him and the accursed warrior to travel away from the camp.\n2\tReturn to Artamir at Tham Durlan\tArtamir can be found at Tham Durlan. Mincham has offered tenuous permission for Artamir to speak with the accursed warrior privately, but is concerned that it may endanger the Host of the West.\n3\tSeek Artamir and the accursed warrior to the north of Tham Durlan\tArtamir can be found somewhere to the north of Tham Durlan. Artamir fled the camp while you spoke to Mincham and has now gone missing along with the accursed warrior. You should seek him at once.\n4\tTalk to Artamir outside Ondoher's Folly\tArtamir can be found in hiding outside of Ondoher's Folly. You have found Artamir and the accursed warrior and should now confront him about leaving before Mincham's permission was granted.\n5\tFaramir, son of Ondoher can be found to the north of Tham Durlan near the entrance to Ondoher's Folly in Dagorlad. Artamir has spoken to the spirit of Faramir, son of Ondoher, and believes that what he has seen may be of use to the Host of the West. You should learn more of Faramir's burdens.\t\n6\tTalk to Artamir outside Ondoher's Folly\tArtamir can be found on the plains to the south of Ondoher's Folly. You have learned much of Faramir's tragic past as well as the new foes that have risen against the Host of the West. You should now speak to Artamir and urge him to tell the Rangers of what you both have learned.\n",
[14453]="700529CF\n1\tDestroy goblin watch-towers (total: 8)\tGoblin watch-towers have been erected between Vegbár and Goblin-town. You should destroy goblin watch-towers so you can enter Goblin-town unnoticed.\n2\tCompleted\tYou destroyed some of the hastily-erected watch-towers.\n",
[14454]="7004A8CE\n1\tFrodo and Sam's belongings can be found in the watch-tower of Lugvarg in the eastern reaches of Rath Cail. Legolas has asked you to investigate Lugvarg and recover any belongings of Frodo and Sam that you find.\t\n2\tDeliver the cloak and damaged pots to Legolas in Rath Cail\tLegolas can be found in Rath Cail. You have found a tattered cloak that one of the hobbits wore during the journey through Mordor as well as Samwise Gamgee's pots. You should deliver them to Legolas.\n",
[14455]="7003A5F3\n1\tScout the Stair of the Hold\030Scout the road to the Hornburg\tThe road to the Hornburg can be found to the south-west of Underharrow, and the Stair of the Hold can be found to the south-east. Ellen Fremedon has asked you to scout the roads for threats to her people.\n2\tTalk to Ellen Fremedon\tEllen Fremedon can be found outside the Mead Hall of Underharrow. You have scouted the roads away from Underharrow and found them free of the Enemy. You should return to Ellen Fremedon.\n",
[14456]="70047E09\n1\tBurn banners at Ondoher's Folly (total: 8)\tBanners can be found throughout Ondoher's Folly in north-western Dagorlad. You have discovered many banners of the Eye flying at Ondoher's Folly. You should burn them and loosen the Enemy's grip on the Wastes.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have burned many of the Enemy's banners at Ondoher's Folly.\n",
[14457]="7003E2B0\n1\tDefeat crebain in Nan Wathren (total: 15)\tCrebain can be found in Nan Wathren, in the southern North Downs. You should defeat the cruel crebain of Nan Wathren. Small fellowship recommended.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated a number of crebain from Nan Wathren.\n",
[14458]="7006212F\n1\tWatcyn's lost belongings should be scattered around the stairs in Caranost, west of Sírlond.\t\n2\tTalk to Watcyn\tYou have reclaimed Watcyn's belongings -- or, at least, whatever was left. You should return to Watcyn in Sírlond.\n3\tTalk to Rendal\tWatcyn has asked you to split some of his coin between you and Rendal. Rendal has returned to Sírlond by now.\n",
[14459]="70048C98\n1\tTBD\tTBD Go to Agarnaith Ranger Camp\n2\tTBD Speak with Ranger 1\t\n",
[14460]="7006BF80\n1\tGo to the marketplace outside the Well of Forgetting\tGo to the marketplace outside Tûl Zakana, the Well of Forgetting, and barter for some of their water with the coin Usakâr gave you. Tûl Zakana is far to the east of Dag Usakâra. It can be found south-east of the Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi.\n2\tBarter for some water with the Shagâni man behind the counter\tTalk to the Shagâni man behind the counter, and barter for some of their water.\n3\tFight off the attackers and flee toward the hills\tFight off the attackers and flee up the hill!\n4\tReturn to Usakâr at Dag Usakâra\tReturn to Usakâr at Dag Usakâra and tell him what happened.\n",
[14461]="700717A3\n1\tGather water (total: 3)\030Inspect diseased fish\030Inspect diseased insects\tIrsinith has asked that you check the marsh near the Hill of the Mother for how the blight has hurt the water and wildlife. She requested you bring her some water samples as well.\n2\tBring gathered water to Irsinith\tReturn to Irisinith with the water you have gathered from the nearby marsh and tell her what you witnessed of the blight's destruction.\n",
[14462]="7000850D\n1\tCollect water at the banner-marked pools (total: 6)\tThe banner-marked pools are spread throughout western Malenhad. Murdaigán has asked you to go to six springs in the swamp and collect samples of water which he can use to confirm whether those springs have not yet been poisoned by the filth of Angmar.\n2\tTalk to Murdaigán\030Collect Full Water-skin (total: 6)\tMurdaigán is back at the hunters' camp in the south-west corner of Malenhad. Having collected several water samples, you should bring them back to Murdaigán.\n",
[14463]="7002D4EF\n1\tCollect a bucket of well-water\tThe well for water can be found in the centre of Combe, near the horse's stall.\n",
[14464]="7000BEE3\n1\tTalk to Eywind\tEywind is at his camp with Nogmeldir, at the entrance to the High Pass. Nogmeldir suggested you speak with Eywind concerning the Wargs and what the dwarves know of them.\n2\tTalk to Thorgest\tThe dwarf brothers are said to dwell at Hrimbarg, to the east and a bit south of Vindurhal. Eywind suggested you find the dwarf-brothers he spoke of and ask them what they know of the Wargs of the Misty Mountains.\n3\tTalk to Nogmeldir\tNogmeldir is at Vindurhal, a little north and to the west of Hrimbarg. You should return to Nogmeldir and tell him what you have learned of the Wargs.\n",
})
